        "answer": {
          "short": "A downward-opening parabola whose vertex has the same $x$-coordinate as the $x$-intercept of the gradient graph.",
          "worked": "Let $c$ be the $x$-intercept of the gradient graph. The straight gradient graph has nonzero slope, so $f$ is quadratic. The gradient changes from positive to zero to negative at $x=c$, so the parabola opens downwards and its vertex is a maximum at $x=c$.",
